#question(title: [True, False, or Shrug?], shrink: true)[
  #set text(size: 11pt)

  We want to find a function $H$ with domain
  $RR$ such that $display(H(1) = - 2)$ and
  such that $display(H' (x) = e^(sin x))$ for
  all $x$. Decide whether each of the
  following statements is true, false, or we
  do not have enough information to decide.

  + The function
    $display(quad H(x) = integral_0^x e^(sin t) d t quad)$
    is a solution.
  + The function
    $display(quad H(x) = integral_2^x e^(sin t) d t quad)$
    is a solution.
  + $forall C in RR$, the function
    $display(quad H(x) = integral_0^x e^(sin t) d t + C quad)$
    is a solution.
  + $exists C in RR$ s.t. the function
    $display(quad H(x) = integral_0^x e^(sin t) d t + C quad)$
    is a solution.
  + The function
    $display(quad H(x) = integral_1^x e^(sin t) d t - 2 quad)$
    is a solution.
  + There is more than one solution.
]
